PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
Unanimous consensus across all 18 panel members remains firmly established on Choice A. Under Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium with no gene-environment correlation, phenotypic variance decomposes orthogonally, strictly capping the predictive power of any genetic predictor at broad-sense heritability ($H^2 = 0.50$). Statements B, C, and D are not necessarily true because non-additive genetic effects are neither guaranteed nor precluded, and environmental epigenetic effects do not restrict narrow-sense heritability. With Statement A uniquely satisfying deductive necessity, Choice A is the direct and correct answer.
}

